  "overview_markdown": "OpenClaw is the reference open-source personal AI assistant: a single Gateway process runs on your own hardware and connects you to Discord, iMessage, Slack, Teams, Telegram, WhatsApp, and 20+ other channels, plus native apps for macOS, iOS, Android, Windows, and Linux. State, memory, and credentials live locally; model providers and agent harnesses (Claude, Codex, local models) are swappable plugins, and the same binary scales from a laptop assistant to a shared team deployment with only configuration changes.\n\nThe architecture follows a 'trusted gateway, untrusted execution, deterministic policy' model, with telemetry limited to an opt-out daily version check and opt-in anonymous statistics. Recent commits show heavy investment in reliability: durable progress-attachment custody across restarts, host-owned SQLite brokers for session lifecycle, doctor/migration repair tooling, and CI policy hardening — evidence of a maturing, production-grade codebase.\n\nAs the upstream project, OpenClaw defines the category that clones (Hermes, Muse, BetterClaw, AnyClaw) differentiate against. Its strengths are ecosystem breadth (5,400+ community skills), a foundation-governed MIT license with no paid tier, and an aggressive release cadence (v2026.9.x with atomic updates and plugin hot reloading). Trade-offs include a Node.js resource footprint, occasional regressions from fast shipping, and setup complexity for non-technical users.",
